+# Recurring Act34 envelope — technical candidate (2026-11-24)
+
+**Status: DRAFT ARTIFACTS ONLY.** Nothing here is installed, signed, activated,
+attested or dispatched. Canonical `government/knowledge-budget.conf`,
+`records/knowledge/activation.json`, the four signed permits and the 45-day
+ledger are untouched. No office was signed for or activated by this work.
+Prepared under handoff `H-1795550506-92c3`. All numbers below are reproducible
+with `python3 verify.py` against the live read-only government primitives.
+
+## 1. Problem (from the real first wave)
+
+Four reservations closed in canonical state (`knowledge/budget/reservations/`),
+all `cost: 0.0`, `cost_reported: true`, config `0964bd1e…`:
+
+| office | tokens | CPU-s (whole-host UPPER_BOUND) | wall-s | exit |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| statistics | 3,257,367 | 3,549.29 | 871 | clearexit |
+| foresight | 3,163,657 | 3,161.12 | 791 | clearexit |
+| strategy | 2,509,129 | 3,100.00 | 773 | clearexit |
+| spying | 0 | 1,969.39 | 484 | terminal_unknown (runner recovery) |
+
+Aggregate: **8,930,153 tokens / 11,779.8 CPU-s / 2,919 wall-s**, cost 0.
+`aggregate.json` on disk was independently reconstructed by
+`knowledge-budget-tool.py aggregate` from all four rows — exact match.
+
+The live config sets each office's `per_run_caps` **equal** to its 45-day `caps`
+(11,320,103 / 7,987 / 1,997). `admit()` projects `office_used + per_run_cap`,
+so every second reservation is mechanically refused (`admit_current_real`:
+false for all four). The debt is not the problem — the per-run ceiling is.
+
+## 2. Candidate envelope — distinct cumulative and per-run caps
+
+Act34 §3(5) and the Economy follow-on plan fix the **cumulative** envelope at
+`max(proxy p95, observed max)`. Observed maxima are all below the proxy p95, so
+cumulative caps are **unchanged**: per office 11,320,103 tokens / 7,987 CPU-s
+UPPER_BOUND / 1,997 wall-s; aggregate 45,280,412 / 31,948 / 7,988. Window stays
+45 days (3,888,000 s). The ledger is never reset or rebranded.
+
+New, distinct **per-run caps**, uniform across offices:
+
+| metric | per run | basis |
+|---|---:|---|
+| accounting tokens | 3,300,000 | just above observed max 3,257,367; ~95% is cache-read |
+| CPU-s (whole-host UPPER_BOUND) | 2,200 | ≤ observed max 3,549; ≈ 4 fully-busy cores × 550 wall-s |
+| wall-s | 550 | within observed 484–871 range; 1 concurrent run/office |
+
+Remaining headroom (cumulative cap − real ledger charge) that this must fit:
+
+| office | tokens | CPU-s | wall-s |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| statistics | 8,062,736 | 4,437.71 | 1,126 |
+| foresight | 8,156,446 | 4,825.88 | 1,206 |
+| strategy | 8,810,974 | 4,887.00 | 1,224 |
+| spying | 11,320,103 | 6,017.61 | 1,513 |
+| aggregate | 36,350,259 | 20,168.20 | 5,069 |
+
+This is a **bounded recurrence**, not an unlimited one: the candidate admits the
+next turn and one further turn for every office, then the third is refused by the
+same fail-closed code (wall/CPU/tokens headroom exhausted). That is deliberate —
+multiple regular turns inside the enacted 45-day term, without raising a cap,
+resetting debt, or extending authority.
+
+## 3. Verification against authoritative code and adverse cases
+
+Run with the unchanged `knowledge-budget-tool.py`, `knowledge-practical-bounds.py`
+and the real ledger rows; full outputs in `evidence/results/`. The full test suite
+was **not** rerun.
+
+| check | result |
+|---|---|
+| draft config `validate` | ok (per-run ≤ cumulative; window 45 d; aggregate ≥ office) |
+| current config `admit` on real ledger | refused for all 4 (the reported defect) |
+| draft config `admit` on real ledger | admitted for all 4 |
+| 2nd follow-on turn (1 charged) | admitted for all 4 |
+| 3rd follow-on turn (2 charged) | refused for all 4 (headroom exhausted) |
+| 399,000 used / 400,000 cap / 120,000 run | refused (cumulative repeat guard) |
+| 120,000 used / 400,000 cap / 120,000 run | admitted (genuine recurrence) |
+| missing `by_office` | refused ("missing per-office liability") |
+| negative/invalid accounting | refused (fail closed) |
+| `per_run_caps > cumulative caps` | config `validate` rejects |
+| `overrun` at tokens == cap | `over: true` (stop-on-detection, not a hard cap) |
+| CPU baseline reboot | rejected ("CPU host rebooted during reservation") |
+| ambiguous exit | `state: held`, full 3,300,000/2,200/550 retained, `released: 0` |
+
+Artifacts: `knowledge-budget.conf` (draft), `permits/*.json` (unsigned;
+`budget_sha256=82069b27…`, same unchanged Economy control hashes/digest),
+`generate-unsigned-permits.py`, `verify.py`, `evidence/`.
+
+## 4. Resource, funding and privacy facts (not instructions)
+
+- Funding: 4/13 free models available at 18:41Z, `funding_risk=none`; 10 exact
+  allowlist IDs cooling until ~00:53Z 2026-11-25; failover `elevated`; 1 Luna
+  fallback exists but is **not** admitted. All currently available routes are
+  `opencode-go`, so the "two independent free routes" condition is only weakly
+  met (two source-verified allowlisted IDs, `hy4-flash-free` + `hungerg-free`,
+  sharing one provider). No paid/Luna spend, no data-scope change.
+- Host: 4 CPUs, load ~16 (contended), memory ~6 GiB spare (`ok`), disk `short`.
+  `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` disk line is unchanged and not repeated here.
+- Privacy: zero-billed exact-ID allowlist + `knowledge-free-dispatch.sh`
+  prelaunch `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` pin; negative-acceptance digest
+  `b5f40a2a…`; Spying source scope unchanged. None of these controls change.
+
+## 5. Genuine officer approval that is REQUIRED
+
+The permit JSONs here are candidates with `signature_status: unsigned` and
+`signer: null`. A self-labelled `signed` flag is **not** a signature: the gate's
+`institutionally_attested(..., historical=True)` requires real board review bound
+to the exact origin commit and digest. Specifically:
+
+1. **Executive (`c1e00002`)** — record four written, timestamped, reversible
+   follow-on permits, land config + permits + `activation.json`
+   (`permit_sha256`/`permit_origin_commit`/`permit_attestation`) in one reviewed
+   main commit, and file genuine attestations for `act34-executive-<office>`.
+2. **Economy (`c1e00012`)** — publish the measured recurring-envelope report in
+   `records/economy/` from this evidence (observed rows + wave IDs) and supply the
+   attested `act34-economy-free-provider-control` evidence. The eight control
+   hashes/digest are unchanged, so the 18:31Z attestation bundle remains reusable.
+3. **Judiciary (`c1e00008`)** — file an after-start `proceed` review within 48 h
+   of each new permit start, bound to the new permit hash and attested for
+   `act34-judiciary-<office>`; `hold`/`stop`/no filing suspends dispatch.
+4. No Founder approval is sought for new spending (there is none); the existing
+   disk `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` line is unchanged. Affirmative reauthorisation at the
+   45-day expiry still applies.
+
+## 6. Candidate path (delivered via handoff to Economy + Executive)
+
+Economy publishes the measured envelope → Executive signs and lands the four
+permits + config + activation bindings (no waiting on parity legislation) →
+Judiciary files the post-start review → gates PASS → dispatch resumes under the
+distinct per-run caps with 20 s monitoring, `overrun_action: kill`, and the
+non-resettable cumulative ledger. Spying preflight and the zero-billed path stay
+enforced. If a cap/permit change cannot be lawfully evidenced, hold; do not
+fabricate an attestation or activate on these draft bytes.
